{"term": "va te faire foutre", "lang": "fr", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "insults", "subcategory": "expletive", "concept": "fucker_insult", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 92, "technical": 0, "recognition_pct_current": 99, "recognition_pct_peak": 99, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Imperative expletive meaning 'go fuck yourself'; the standard French all-purpose dismissal equivalent to 'fuck you' or 'go fuck yourself'.", "english_term": "go fuck yourself", "english_translation_quality": "direct", "notes": "Literally 'go get yourself fucked'; built from the reflexive of 'foutre' (to fuck). Ubiquitous across registers of French profanity; tone ranges from furious to dismissively contemptuous."}
{"term": "branleur", "lang": "fr", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "insults", "subcategory": "masturbation_insult", "concept": "fucker_insult", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 72, "technical": 0, "recognition_pct_current": 96, "recognition_pct_peak": 96, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "A lazy, worthless good-for-nothing; literally 'one who masturbates'; the closest French equivalent of British 'wanker'.", "english_term": "wanker", "english_translation_quality": "direct", "notes": "From 'branler' (to masturbate). As an insult the primary connotation is uselessness and idleness rather than sexual deviance. Feminine form 'branleuse' exists but is rarer."}
